Package: surveyIDmasker
Title: Mask Participant Identifiers in Survey Exports
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R:
    person("Francesco", "Zanibellato", email = "fz150@georgetown.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Replaces participant identifiers in survey data files
    ('Prolific', 'CloudResearch Connect' and 'MTurk' IDs, IP addresses,
    locations, emails, phone numbers) with codes prefixed by "MSK", made by
    encrypting each value with a private key (AES-256). Data can be shared
    without disclosing identities while repeated participants remain
    recognizable, also across several files masked with the same key, and the
    authors, who keep the key, can turn the codes back into the original
    identifiers. Locations and IP addresses can keep their country (and US
    state). Reads and writes CSV, 'SPSS' (.sav), 'Stata' (.dta) and 'Excel'
    (.xlsx) files, such as exports from 'Qualtrics' or 'Credamo' and lab data
    files, keeping header rows and variable labels.
